# descent-vk player ship
#
# A flattened arrowhead: a single hexagonal cross-section swept from a nose
# point back to a tail cap, with the left and right vertices of that hexagon
# pushed out far enough to read as wings. 22 triangles.
#
# THIS MESH MUST STAY CLOSED. Every edge is shared by exactly two triangles,
# with no boundary edge anywhere. M3 extrudes silhouette edges into stencil
# shadow volumes and depth-fail counting is only correct for a closed mesh; the
# loader treats an open edge as a fatal asset error. Adding detail here means
# adding it as closed geometry, not as a loose flap or an inserted triangle.
#
# Local frame matches the renderer: -Z forward, +Y up, +X right. Triangles wind
# counter-clockwise seen from outside. Normals are not authored; the loader
# computes flat per-face normals so the hull reads as faceted.

# nose
v  0.00  0.00 -3.00

# mid ring, z = 0: right wingtip, top pair, left wingtip, bottom pair
v  2.00  0.00  0.00
v  0.50  0.35  0.00
v -0.50  0.35  0.00
v -2.00  0.00  0.00
v -0.50 -0.35  0.00
v  0.50 -0.35  0.00

# tail ring, z = 1.40, same order, tapered
v  1.40  0.00  1.40
v  0.42  0.30  1.40
v -0.42  0.30  1.40
v -1.40  0.00  1.40
v -0.42 -0.30  1.40
v  0.42 -0.30  1.40

vt 0.00 0.00
vt 1.00 0.00
vt 1.00 1.00
vt 0.00 1.00
vt 0.50 1.00

# nose fan
f 1/1 3/2 2/5
f 1/1 4/2 3/5
f 1/1 5/2 4/5
f 1/1 6/2 5/5
f 1/1 7/2 6/5
f 1/1 2/2 7/5

# hull sides, mid ring to tail ring
f 2/1 3/2 9/3
f 2/1 9/3 8/4
f 3/1 4/2 10/3
f 3/1 10/3 9/4
f 4/1 5/2 11/3
f 4/1 11/3 10/4
f 5/1 6/2 12/3
f 5/1 12/3 11/4
f 6/1 7/2 13/3
f 6/1 13/3 12/4
f 7/1 2/2 8/3
f 7/1 8/3 13/4

# tail cap
f 8/1 9/2 10/3
f 8/1 10/2 11/3
f 8/1 11/2 12/3
f 8/1 12/2 13/3
